assistant_response:
In Java, you can sort an array of integers efficiently using the `Arrays.sort()` method. This is the standard approach for sorting primitive arrays. Here's an example of how you can use it:

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

public class ArraySorter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] data = {9, 4, 7, 2, 5, 1, 8, 3, 6};
        System.out.println("Original array: " + Arrays.toString(data));

        Arrays.sort(data); // Utilizes the built-in sorting algorithm

        System.out.println("Sorted array: " + Arrays.toString(data));
    }
}
```

This method sorts the array elements in ascending order by default. For more complex sorting scenarios involving objects, you would typically pass a `Comparator`.

